  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome, but neither lottery has one, so the reason would not favor either. However, the individual does not refer to the concept of a sure outcome or certainty at any point. Instead, the justification is based on the perceived similarity of the lotteries and a consequent random choice. There is no indication that the individual analyzed the lotteries in terms of whether an outcome was certain. The information considered (similarity) and the justification (random choice due to similarity) do not align with the decision reason’s focus (presence of sure outcome). Therefore, there is no evidence the reason was used in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
